cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fox in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "fox: a local LLM inference server for concurrent workloads"
abstract: >-
  fox is an inference server written in Rust that wraps llama.cpp and serves GGUF
  models over OpenAI- and Ollama-compatible HTTP APIs. It is built around reuse of
  already-computed KV cache: sequences retain the tokens they hold, arriving requests
  skip the prefill for whatever prefix they share, and concurrent requests can copy a
  shared prefix out of a sequence that is still decoding rather than each prefilling
  it and each reserving a copy of its blocks.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lemos
    given-names: "Manuel S."
repository-code: "https://github.com/ferrumox/fox"
license:
